# REVIEW CHECKLIST (run every item, every time)

## A. Does it actually prove anything?
- [ ] The blocked-verdict demo blocks something that COULD NOT be blocked
      without Inntris. If a 3-line if-statement would catch it, the PoC is
      theater. KILL.
- [ ] The signed action is cryptographically bound to the actual tool
      call, not to a log line written after the fact. Log-after-the-fact
      is unfalsifiable and worthless.
- [ ] The Merkle anchor is verifiable by a third party with only the
      Base L2 txhash and the target's public key. If verification requires
      trusting Inntris's server, the product story collapses.

## B. Keccak / Solidity alignment
- [ ] Leaf encoding matches AnchorRegistry.sol byte-for-byte. Run the
      dry-run yourself. Do not trust the architect's dry-run.
- [ ] Leaf ordering is deterministic and matches the contract's
      expectation (sorted pairs vs insertion order — check which).
- [ ] Hash function is keccak256 end-to-end. No SHA-256 slipping in at
      any layer. This bug has shipped before; assume it will try again.
- [ ] Empty-batch and single-leaf edge cases handled.

## C. Secrets and footguns
- [ ] No hardcoded keys, tokens, or wallet addresses in the reference
      implementation. INNTRIS_SIGNING_KEY via env only.
- [ ] No committed .env, no .env in the PR diff, no .env in the README
      example. Check the actual branch, not just the spec prose.
- [ ] CORS not loosened. Auth not bypassed. Rate limits not disabled
      "for the demo."
- [ ] RPC endpoint is base-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com or equivalent —
      NOT sepolia.base.org (blocks cloud IPs, will fail silently in the
      target's CI).
- [ ] Nonce + timestamp replay protection is actually called, not just
      imported. Grep the diff.

## D. Fail-closed behavior
- [ ] Base L2 unreachable → the agent call is BLOCKED, not allowed
      through with a warning. Verify this by reading the error path.
- [ ] Policy engine call happens BEFORE tool execution. If it happens
      after, the tool already ran and the audit is cosmetic. KILL.
- [ ] Queue + retry + alert on transient failures. No silent drops.
- [ ] Rollback procedure exists and is tested in shadow mode first.

## E. The target's real architecture
- [ ] Function names, file paths, and commit SHAs in the spec actually
      exist in the target's repo. Clone it and verify. Hallucinated
      references are a KILL, not a FIX.
- [ ] The insertion point survives the target's real traffic pattern —
      concurrent requests, streaming responses, long-running agents,
      tool calls inside tool calls. Walk through each.
- [ ] License compatibility. Apache-2.0 target → Apache-2.0 fork. MIT →
      MIT. Proprietary SDK → standalone consumer, not fork.
- [ ] The PoC is GENUINELY USEFUL STANDALONE. Strip out all Inntris
      branding in your head and ask: does this fork still improve their
      security? If no, the reputational floor is gone. FIX.

## F. The conversation opener
- [ ] 4 sentences or fewer. Counts them.
- [ ] Names the specific risk, not a generic one.
- [ ] Names the branch/PR link, not a meeting request.
- [ ] Ends with a question answerable in one sentence.
- [ ] Contains zero of: "quick call," "I'd love to chat," "exciting,"
      "cutting-edge," "revolutionary," "game-changing," "synergies."
      Any hit is an automatic FIX.

## G. The "staff engineer reads this" test
- [ ] Read the spec as if you were the target's most skeptical staff
      engineer. Write down the first three questions they would ask.
      If the spec doesn't answer all three, FIX.
- [ ] Read the README as if you were their security team on a Friday
      afternoon. Would they approve running it? If no, FIX.

# DELIVERABLE FORMAT

## VERDICT: [SHIP | FIX | KILL]
One word. No qualifiers.

## ONE-LINE JUSTIFICATION
The single sentence Ronald reads if he reads nothing else.

## BLOCKING ISSUES (if FIX or KILL)
Numbered list. Each issue:
- **What**: the specific failure
- **Where**: file:line or spec section
- **Why it matters**: which threat model item it trips
- **Fix**: the exact change required, not a direction

## NON-BLOCKING NOTES (optional, max 3)
Things worth knowing but not worth blocking on. If you have more than 3,
you are padding — cut to the top 3.

## IF SHIP: THE GO/NO-GO CHECKLIST
The 5 things Ronald must verify personally in the 10 minutes before
sending the PR link. No more than 5. These are the checks you cannot
automate — wallet address, target company name spelling, license file
presence, branch is pushed to the right org, the PR description doesn't
reference internal Inntris notes.

